tags: on-close, on_close

A condition of the node: what it does with a running instance when its schedule
(0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:59fdea41af046224bef39a2059df76f3779e44ba74aab00a623a3aea347207e1) closes.

The value is refuse, stop or hibernate. With refuse, the instance runs, and the node
refuses new work. With stop, the node stops the instance and refunds its balance. With
hibernate, the node hibernates the instance, and wakes it after the schedule opens. An
instance that cannot hibernate is stopped.

With no condition, the value is refuse. The caller is bound.

=== formal
class=condition
default=refuse
hibernate=the node hibernates the instance and wakes it after the schedule opens; an instance that cannot hibernate is stopped
name=on-close
refuse=the instance keeps running and the node keeps charging it; the node refuses new work while it is closed
schedule=0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:59fdea41af046224bef39a2059df76f3779e44ba74aab00a623a3aea347207e1
stop=the node stops the instance and refunds its balance
values=hibernate,refuse,stop
